---
description: "Pydantic schema rules (validation, typing, boundaries)"
globs:
  - "**/*schema*.py"
  - "**/*model*.py"
  - "**/schemas/**/*.py"
  - "**/models/**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Pydantic Rules
- Use explicit typed fields with meaningful names.
- Validate data at boundaries with Pydantic models.
- Avoid passing raw dict payloads across layers when a model exists.
- Keep model validators focused and deterministic.
- Prefer clear domain models over generic payload containers.
